\newlabel{fig:frames}{{1}{2}{Three consecutive fixed-exposure reference frames (100~ms, white balance locked at 5600~K, solar-keyed night gain $86\to 87\to 87$), night of 8--9 August 2026. Fixed artificial sources are stable across the triplet (lamp cores $>220$: $246\to 245\to 236$; lit windows show only additive sky-reflected fill), ruling out an exposure or gain excursion: the middle frame records real, additive, sky-borne light}{figure.caption.1}{}}
