\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces 4K pixel-level radiometric diagnostics across the top-25\% sky band of the flash frame, binned by flash blue digital number ($B_{\rm  DN}$). (a)~Standard sRGB linearization leaves a $+6.3\%$ brightness-dependent drift in $R/G$, which disappears when linearized with the camera's independently calibrated per-channel empirical CRF. (b)~Both linearizations show monotonic $B/G$ compression above $B_{\rm  DN}\approx 220$ from the ISP highlight shoulder and partial blue clipping ($1.04\%$ of the sky band at $B\ge 254$).}}{3}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:radiometry}{{2}{3}{4K pixel-level radiometric diagnostics across the top-25\% sky band of the flash frame, binned by flash blue digital number ($B_{\rm DN}$). (a)~Standard sRGB linearization leaves a $+6.3\%$ brightness-dependent drift in $R/G$, which disappears when linearized with the camera's independently calibrated per-channel empirical CRF. (b)~Both linearizations show monotonic $B/G$ compression above $B_{\rm DN}\approx 220$ from the ISP highlight shoulder and partial blue clipping ($1.04\%$ of the sky band at $B\ge 254$)}{figure.caption.2}{}}
