\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Camera-pipeline validation against the monitor's own daytime archive (fixed WB~5600~K) and resulting 3-component lightning mixture solves for the flash ($R/G=1.028$, $B/G=1.854$, 3~km Rayleigh). Un-matrixed Bayer fails on clear blue sky and forces a spurious 12--19\% N$_2^+${} requirement; restoring the CCM (or CIE-sRGB) matches daytime skies and favors optically thin Kramers continuum with weak or zero N$_2^+${}. Negative weights (\emph  {infeasible}) indicate the target lies outside the non-negative simplex.}}{5}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:validation}{{1}{5}{Camera-pipeline validation against the monitor's own daytime archive (fixed WB~5600~K) and resulting 3-component lightning mixture solves for the flash ($R/G=1.028$, $B/G=1.854$, 3~km Rayleigh). Un-matrixed Bayer fails on clear blue sky and forces a spurious 12--19\% \Ntp {} requirement; restoring the CCM (or CIE-sRGB) matches daytime skies and favors optically thin Kramers continuum with weak or zero \Ntp {}. Negative weights (\emph {infeasible}) indicate the target lies outside the non-negative simplex}{table.caption.3}{}}
\citation{orville1968,orvillehenderson1984,walker2019}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces (a)~Best-fit CIE-sRGB emission model on a log--linear scale ($(w_c,w_a,w_m)=(0.57,0.38,0.05)$ with 30\,000~K optically thin Kramers continuum), with every modeled line labeled alongside the approximate Bayer passbands (670~nm IR-cut, 398~nm UV edge). (b)~Colorimetric closure and archive validation in linear $(R/G,B/G)$ space. Archive clear blue sky ($n=288$, blue triangle) refutes the un-matrixed Bayer model (red cross and dotted ceiling) and validates CIE-sRGB (open blue triangle). In CIE-sRGB, Planck 30\,kK $+$ Atomic (dashed) is too blue, while Kramers 30\,kK $+$ Atomic ($w_m=0$, solid purple) passes beside all three flash estimates (top-25\% sRGB star, empirical CRF diamond, unclipped sky open circle; shaded wedge adds $w_m\le 0.15$). Removing H$\alpha $ (red dot) makes $R/G>1$ unreachable.}}{6}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spectrum}{{3}{6}{(a)~Best-fit CIE-sRGB emission model on a log--linear scale ($(w_c,w_a,w_m)=(0.57,0.38,0.05)$ with 30\,000~K optically thin Kramers continuum), with every modeled line labeled alongside the approximate Bayer passbands (670~nm IR-cut, 398~nm UV edge). (b)~Colorimetric closure and archive validation in linear $(R/G,B/G)$ space. Archive clear blue sky ($n=288$, blue triangle) refutes the un-matrixed Bayer model (red cross and dotted ceiling) and validates CIE-sRGB (open blue triangle). In CIE-sRGB, Planck 30\,kK $+$ Atomic (dashed) is too blue, while Kramers 30\,kK $+$ Atomic ($w_m=0$, solid purple) passes beside all three flash estimates (top-25\% sRGB star, empirical CRF diamond, unclipped sky open circle; shaded wedge adds $w_m\le 0.15$). Removing H$\alpha $ (red dot) makes $R/G>1$ unreachable}{figure.caption.4}{}}
